    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p56-q9-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{2\\pi}9\\right)+\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{4\\pi}9\\right)+\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{8\\pi}9\\right)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0$.",
          "worked": "By the sum of roots of $8x^3+0x^2-6x+1=0$,\n$$\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma=-\\frac08=0.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p56-q9-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{2\\pi}9\\right)\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{4\\pi}9\\right)\\cos\\left(\\dfrac{8\\pi}9\\right)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\dfrac18$.",
          "worked": "By the product of roots,\n$$\\alpha\\beta\\gamma=-\\frac18.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p56-q9-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\cos^2\\left(\\dfrac{2\\pi}9\\right)+\\cos^2\\left(\\dfrac{4\\pi}9\\right)+\\cos^2\\left(\\dfrac{8\\pi}9\\right)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac32$.\n\nUse $(\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma)^2-2(\\alpha\\beta+\\alpha\\gamma+\\beta\\gamma)$.",
          "worked": "From the coefficients,\n$$\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma=0,\\qquad\\alpha\\beta+\\alpha\\gamma+\\beta\\gamma=-\\frac68=-\\frac34.$$\nTherefore,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\alpha^2+\\beta^2+\\gamma^2&=(\\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma)^2-2(\\alpha\\beta+\\alpha\\gamma+\\beta\\gamma)\\\\\\alpha^2+\\beta^2+\\gamma^2&=0^2-2\\left(-\\frac34\\right)\\\\\\alpha^2+\\beta^2+\\gamma^2&=\\frac32.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p56-q9-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$\\sec\\left(\\dfrac{2\\pi}9\\right)+\\sec\\left(\\dfrac{4\\pi}9\\right)+\\sec\\left(\\dfrac{8\\pi}9\\right)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$6$.\n\nWrite the secants as reciprocal roots and use the pairwise-product sum divided by the product.",
          "worked": "Since $\\sec\\theta=\\frac{1}{\\cos\\theta}$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1\\alpha+\\frac1\\beta+\\frac1\\gamma&=\\frac{\\beta\\gamma+\\alpha\\gamma+\\alpha\\beta}{\\alpha\\beta\\gamma}\\\\\\frac1\\alpha+\\frac1\\beta+\\frac1\\gamma&=\\frac{-3/4}{-1/8}\\\\\\frac1\\alpha+\\frac1\\beta+\\frac1\\gamma&=6.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 38
      }
    ]
  },
